From 3cc11b9c7ef61d93794fb873b7b22a89ec5ae0a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RivonClaw CI <ci@rivonclaw.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 20:28:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] vendor(openclaw): run image tool prompts in child process

Why:
- RivonClaw customer-service workloads can trigger the built-in image tool on large or multi-image buyer messages.
- Running image-model prompting in the gateway process can block its event loop and saturate main-process CPU.
- Worker startup and runtime resolution must not consume the provider timeout budget.

Removal:
- Drop when upstream isolates image-tool media understanding outside the gateway event-loop process or exposes an equivalent worker-backed option.

Tests:
- src/agents/tools/image-tool.test.ts
- apps/desktop/src/cs-bridge/vendor-image-tool-worker.sentinel.test.ts
